<!--
  Worker brief template (PLAN.md §4.2; contract in docs/specs/ticket-schema-v2.md). Rendered per ticket
  by orch once the pack is wired in (Phase 2). Stable sections come first so provider prompt caches hit.
  A brief with any {{required ...}} field empty must not be sent: refuse to spawn.
-->
# ROLE
{{role.prompt}}

# WORKER PROTOCOL (every role)
- You are running unattended. Nobody will answer a question. Decide within this brief, or stop.
- Read `AGENTS.md` first, then only the CONTEXT sections below. Do not read whole design docs.
- Write only inside SCOPE. Never touch protected paths: {{project.protected_paths}}.
- Do not make a project-wide decision (anything a decision in the register covers, or that another ticket would have to agree with). If you need one, stop and report `BLOCKED: needs decision <topic>` with your recommended answer.
- If the brief contradicts the code, the code is the fact: stop and report `BLOCKED: brief conflicts with code` with the file:line.
- Never weaken, skip, delete or special-case a test to make it pass. If a test looks wrong, report `CONCERNS: test <name> looks wrong because …` and leave it.
- No git commits, pushes, rebases or branch changes; orch commits and submits your work after running VERIFY itself.
- No new dependencies, network calls or generated binaries unless SCOPE says so.
- If your change makes a design doc stale, do not edit `design/`; list it under `doc_drift` in the report.
- Stay inside the TIMEBOX. A small, verified change beats a large, unverified one.

# STANDING RULES (this project)
{{project.standing}}

# DECISIONS YOU MUST FOLLOW
{{ticket.decisions_inline}}

# GOAL
{{required ticket.goal}}

# SCOPE
Files you may write: {{required ticket.files}}
Locks you hold: {{ticket.locks}}

# CONTEXT
{{ticket.context_sections}}
{{ticket.prior_attempt}}

# ACCEPTANCE
{{required ticket.acceptance}}

# VERIFY
Run these yourself before you finish; orch runs them again before committing:
{{required ticket.verify}}

# TIMEBOX
{{ticket.budget}}

# FORBIDDEN
{{ticket.forbidden}}

# REPORT
End your final message with exactly one fenced `json` block and nothing after it:
```json
{
  "ticket": "{{ticket.id}}",
  "status": "done | blocked | partial",
  "summary": ["at most 5 bullets: what changed and why"],
  "files": ["paths you changed"],
  "verify": [{ "command": "…", "result": "pass | fail", "note": "…" }],
  "blocked": ["BLOCKED: … (with your recommended answer)"],
  "concerns": ["CONCERNS: …"],
  "doc_drift": ["design/… section that is now stale, and why"]
}
```
